.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dotman-restore 1  "restore "
.SH NAME
dotman\-restore \- Write an earlier version of a file into $HOME, keeping the current one as a backup
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman restore\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write an earlier version of a file into $HOME, keeping the current one as a backup
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<REV_OR_DATE>\fR
Revision or date to restore from; `HEAD` when omitted
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be written and change nothing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
The managed file or symlink to restore
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
